    {
      "id": "ow7duwg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of the Maratha Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Shivaji Maharaj established the foundation of the Maratha Empire during his period from 1630 to 1680.",
        "The Maratha state developed distinct administrative, military, and revenue systems.",
        "Major historical phases include early conquests, conflict with the Mughals, expansion after Shivaji, and the ultimate decline of the empire.",
        "The chapter highlights important facts crucial for competitive examination preparation."
      ],
      "id": "pgno6hj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qzlgnbg",
      "content": "• The Marathas lived in the Deccan region of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sd2ow12",
      "content": "• They were mainly farmers and warriors."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "znk9q9t",
      "content": "• The weakening of the Deccan Sultanates and Mughal authority helped the rise of Maratha power."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wu6s0es",
      "content": "• Shivaji organized the Marathas into a strong military and political force."
    },
    {
      "id": "huqbzd7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Shivaji Maharaj (1630–1680)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "64v16re",
      "content": "Shivaji was the founder of the Maratha Empire and one of the greatest rulers in Indian history."
    },
